   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The side of each cross section is the vertical distance across R, \\( s = f(x) - g(x) = - 2 x^{2} + 6 x \\).",
         "rule_named": "distance between the boundary curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Because an equilateral triangle with side s has area (sqrt(3)/4) s^2, each cross section has area \\( \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}s^{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "area of the named shape"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The volume is \\( \\int_{0}^{3} \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\left(- 2 x^{2} + 6 x\\right)^{2}\\,dx \\), which equals \\( \\frac{81 \\sqrt{3}}{10} \\).",
